---
import Layout from '../../layouts/LayoutWind.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="How Andropause Works: The Science, Explained – Second Wind"
  description="What testosterone actually does, why it declines with age, and how that shows up in energy, mood, muscle, and sleep. Explained clearly for Indian men."
>

  <section class="g-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="g-eyebrow">How It Works</span>
      <h1>What's actually happening inside your body</h1>
      <p>Not a mystery, not "just aging." A specific, measurable hormonal shift with a name, a cause, and things that help. Here's the short version.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="g-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="g-label">The Why</span>
      <h2 class="g-title">Testosterone declines gradually from your 30s onward</h2>
      <p class="g-sub">From around age 30, most men's total testosterone falls by roughly 1 to 2% a year. It's a normal part of aging, not a disease, but the cumulative effect over a decade or two is real and often shows up before men connect the dots.</p>

      <div class="g-steps">
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">1</div>
          <div><h3>Production slows in the testes</h3><p>The Leydig cells that produce testosterone become less responsive to signals from the brain (the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal axis) over time.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">2</div>
          <div><h3>Free testosterone drops faster than total</h3><p>A protein called SHBG rises with age and binds more testosterone, so the "usable" free testosterone often falls faster than the total number on a lab report suggests.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">3</div>
          <div><h3>Lifestyle factors accelerate it</h3><p>Poor sleep, high body fat, chronic stress, sedentary habits, and excess alcohol all independently lower testosterone, on top of the age-related decline.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">4</div>
          <div><h3>Symptoms build quietly</h3><p>Because the decline is gradual, most men adjust to feeling worse rather than recognising it. That's why symptoms often go unaddressed for years.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="g-section" style="background:var(--bg-mid);">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="g-label">The What</span>
      <h2 class="g-title">The medical term is andropause, or LOH</h2>
      <p class="g-sub">This condition is sometimes called "male menopause" informally, but that name is misleading; female menopause is a relatively abrupt hormonal stop, while this is a slow decline over decades. The accurate medical terms are <strong>andropause</strong> or <strong>late-onset hypogonadism (LOH)</strong>, and both describe the same thing: persistently low testosterone with associated symptoms in adult men.</p>
      <div class="g-cols">
        <div class="g-col">
          <h3>Commonly affected</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Energy levels and stamina</li>
            <li>Muscle mass and strength</li>
            <li>Mood, motivation, and focus</li>
            <li>Sleep quality</li>
            <li>Libido and sexual function</li>
            <li>Body composition (more fat, especially around the belly)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="g-col">
          <h3>What it isn't</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Not a sudden "crash," it builds over years</li>
            <li>Not inevitable decline you have to accept as-is</li>
            <li>Not something to self-diagnose from symptoms alone</li>
            <li>Not fixed by supplements marketed as "testosterone boosters"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="g-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="g-label">The How</span>
      <h2 class="g-title">What actually helps</h2>
      <p class="g-sub">For most men, meaningful improvement starts with a combination of lifestyle changes and, where appropriate, a doctor's evaluation, not any single fix.</p>
      <div class="g-steps">
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">1</div>
          <div><h3>Get a proper diagnosis first</h3><p>A morning total testosterone blood test (repeated once if borderline) is the starting point. Symptoms alone can't confirm low testosterone.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">2</div>
          <div><h3>Strength training and sleep, in that order</h3><p>Resistance training and consistent, sufficient sleep have the strongest evidence for supporting testosterone naturally, ahead of any diet change or supplement.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">3</div>
          <div><h3>Address body composition</h3><p>Excess body fat, especially visceral fat, actively converts testosterone to estrogen. Reducing it often improves levels on its own.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="g-step">
          <div class="g-step-num">4</div>
          <div><h3>Discuss medical options if levels are clinically low</h3><p>If a blood test confirms low testosterone with symptoms, a doctor may discuss treatment options suited to your situation. This is a medical decision, not a self-directed one.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="g-callout">
        <strong>Where to go next:</strong> <a href="/wind/quiz">take the 2-minute symptom check</a> to see how your symptoms line up, or jump straight into the <a href="/wind/guide">full guide</a> by topic.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="g-cta">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Ready to check where you stand?</h2>
      <p>2 minutes, completely private, no login needed.</p>
      <a href="/wind/quiz" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Take the Free Symptom Check →</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style is:global>
  .g-hero { background: var(--bg-mid); padding: 4rem 0 3.5rem; }
  .g-eyebrow { display: inline-block; font-size: .74rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-soft); background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: .35rem .9rem; border-radius: 100px; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .g-hero h1 { font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .g-hero p { font-size: 1.02rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 620px; }

  .g-section { padding: 4rem 0; }
  .g-label { font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg-mid); display: inline-block; padding: .3rem .9rem; border-radius: 99px; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .g-section[style] .g-label { background: #fff; }
  .g-title { font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif; font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .g-sub { font-size: .97rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 2rem; max-width: 680px; }

  .g-steps { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .9rem; }
  .g-step { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: flex-start; background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem; }
  .g-step-num { width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--dark); color: #fff; font-weight: 800; font-size: .9rem; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .g-step h3 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: .35rem; }
  .g-step p { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.6; }

  .g-callout { background: var(--bg-mid); border-left: 4px solid var(--dark); border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .g-callout a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 700; }

  .g-cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .g-col { background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.5rem; }
  .g-col h3 { font-size: .95rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: .85rem; }
  .g-col ul { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .55rem; }
  .g-col li { font-size: .87rem; color: var(--ink-soft); padding-left: 1rem; position: relative; line-height: 1.55; }
  .g-col li::before { content: '•'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--dark); font-weight: 900; }

  .g-cta { background: var(--dark); padding: 3.5rem 0; text-align: center; }
  .g-cta h2 { font-family: 'Archivo', sans-serif; font-size: 1.6rem; font-weight: 900; color: #fff; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .g-cta p { color: #B0B0B0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .g-cta .btn-primary { background: #fff; color: #111; border-color: #fff; }
  .g-cta .btn-primary:hover { background: #E8E8E8; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) { .g-cols { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
